{
  /*
    Every number a witness prints beside a planetary name that is not the
    sum of the Hebrew it prints (planetaryNames.json5, beside this file,
    which cites the witnesses and says who read them). One row a reading,
    keyed by the name's id and the witness's. `printed` is the number on
    the page; `expected` the Hebrew's sum, counted as the reading's
    `count` says (at ordinary values for every row here), so that the
    test can hold each row to the data and fail on one that is no longer
    needed. `whose` says where the difference first appears:
      printing    in this witness, its author's or its printer's: the page
                  cannot tell the two apart.
      inherited   copied from the witness in `from`, which has the same
                  number against the same or a further changed spelling.
      unsettled   the evidence read does not say; `note` says what would.
    Plan 093, "Discrepancies, and whose", 1 to 7; the squares' own
    misprints (its 8 and 9) are not names and are not here.
   */

